:"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Former Iowa State AD calls NIL system 'money laundering'","description":"Former Iowa State athletic director Jamie Pollard delivered a scorching appraisal of college athletics to the Knight Commission, equating NIL as a money-laundering operation.","published":"2026-11-17T19:08:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50512485/former-iowa-state-ad-calls-nil-system-money-laundering","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Purdue rolls with FAA ground stop by taking buses to Iowa","description":"Unable to travel by plane, the Boilermakers rolled with the situation and found some good times on the way.","published":"2026-11-17T11:28:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504665/purdue-faa-ground-stop-bus-iowa","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870967/suntarine-perkins","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suntarine_Perkins"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Suntarine Perkins","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suntarine_Perkins","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:40Z","intro":"Suntarine Margo Perkins (born November 17, 2003) is an American college football linebacker for the Ole Miss Rebels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Perkins attended Raleigh High School in Raleigh, Mississippi. He played linebacker and running back in high school. Over his career he had 267 tackles and 10 sacks on defense. As a senior, he had 2,078 yards and 32 touchdowns. A five star recruit, Perkins committed to the University of Mississippi (Ole Miss) to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Perkins became a starter for Ole Miss during his true freshman season in 2023."}]}}